# The dev box is Windows and the wake-word service runs on a Raspberry Pi.
# A shell script or a systemd unit checked out with CRLF fails on Linux with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M", so pin the line endings that have to
# survive the trip rather than leaving it to each machine's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
